summary:
[reference generation] A courier arrives at a drop point under an overpass and finds a stranger with a cutter instead of a client.

detailed_description:
Grimy cyberpunk street film, anamorphic, photoreal, night, dry air under a concrete deck, sodium-amber and magenta grade.

[Shot 1] Kesh rolls the courier bike in under the overpass deck and stops beside the stacked containers, the engine dying to silence, both feet down on the wet floor, staying on the bike. Rain falls hard at the tunnel mouth behind him and none of it reaches him in here. Mox steps out from between the containers and stops three metres short of his front wheel, a handheld cutter held down at her thigh, powered off and dark. The camera Tracks in low alongside the bike at slow speed and settles into a two-shot, drifting handheld throughout. Kesh (S1), flat and bored, says in English: "Delivery for eleven-forty. Code." His lips close and stay closed while she answers. Mox (S2), light and unhurried, says in English: "Sign here."

[Shot 2] At 00:06.500, cut to a low angle over Kesh's shoulder onto Mox, the camera Arcing around her with small amplitude at slow speed. Kesh (S1) says in English: "That's not the code." Mox (S2) says in English: "No. It isn't." She thumbs the cutter and it ignites into a thin white-hot blade, and lifts it to chest height. Both of their lips close immediately after her final word and stay closed for the rest of the video; neither speaks again. The delivery case stays locked in his gauntlet, sealed and shut, and his hands stay on the handlebars the whole time.

overall_soundscape:
Rain roars at the tunnel mouth behind them and never falls on them, with steady dripping off the deck above and water running in a channel along the wall. The bike's hot metal ticks as it stands. Mox's boots scuff grit on concrete. In the last seconds the cutter spins up into a thin rising whine that holds to the end. Both breathe audibly and there are no words in the track beyond the four spoken lines.

non_diegetic_music:
A single low sustained synth drone, no percussion, thinning away as the cutter ignites.

